# Caddy in front of krystallos: install as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, with your
# domain in place of krystallos.example.com (the host given to admin init).
#
# Caddy gets and renews the certificate itself and redirects HTTP to HTTPS;
# both need ports 80 and 443 open.
#
# What krystallos needs from the proxy is Caddy's default behaviour:
# - Responses of type text/event-stream are flushed to the client at once,
#   so the event stream (SSE) needs no flush_interval.
# - There is no limit on request bodies (no request_body max_size), so pushes
#   of any size go through. The server caps bodies outside /git/ itself.
# - Nothing is cached: Caddy has no response cache unless a plugin adds one.
#   Every read must reach the server to be recorded.
# - Nothing is compressed, as there is no encode directive. If you add one,
#   keep /git/ out of it: git compresses its own packs.
# - No header settings: the server ignores X-Forwarded-* and takes its address
#   from the host fixed at admin init.

krystallos.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
}
